WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.768
Coding Exercise 3 combines row filtering and group
filtering Use

00:00:05.795 --> 00:00:10.902
sales First keep only source rows where price is at
least twenty-five

00:00:11.837 --> 00:00:17.650
Then group the remaining rows by category Calculate
total quantity

00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:23.378
and total revenue for each category After those
groups exist keep

00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:29.358
only categories whose total quantity is greater than
ten Finally sort

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:34.937
with the highest revenue first Think about the order
conceptually before

00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:40.874
you write the clauses The price condition belongs to
individual rows The

00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:46.762
total-quantity condition belongs to groups Run and
Check when you are ready

00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:50.975
If the result does not match verify the placement of
WHERE and

00:00:51.001 --> 00:00:53.462
HAVING before changing the aggregate expressions
